{"title":"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the pattern in the diagram continues, what fraction of eighth triangle would be shaded?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55aac6c624146c44f6a45b961bf3a9c3f8fd89c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(10); draw((0,0)--(12,0)--(6,6sqrt(3))--cycle);  draw((15,0)--(27,0)--(21,6sqrt(3))--cycle); fill((21,0)--(18,3sqrt(3))--(24,3sqrt(3))--cycle,black);  draw((30,0)--(42,0)--(36,6sqrt(3))--cycle); fill((34,0)--(32,2sqrt(3))--(36,2sqrt(3))--cycle,black); fill((38,0)--(36,2sqrt(3))--(40,2sqrt(3))--cycle,black); fill((36,2sqrt(3))--(34,4sqrt(3))--(38,4sqrt(3))--cycle,black);  draw((45,0)--(57,0)--(51,6sqrt(3))--cycle); fill((48,0)--(46.5,1.5sqrt(3))--(49.5,1.5sqrt(3))--cycle,black); fill((51,0)--(49.5,1.5sqrt(3))--(52.5,1.5sqrt(3))--cycle,black); fill((54,0)--(52.5,1.5sqrt(3))--(55.5,1.5sqrt(3))--cycle,black); fill((49.5,1.5sqrt(3))--(48,3sqrt(3))--(51,3sqrt(3))--cycle,black); fill((52.5,1.5sqrt(3))--(51,3sqrt(3))--(54,3sqrt(3))--cycle,black); fill((51,3sqrt(3))--(49.5,4.5sqrt(3))--(52.5,4.5sqrt(3))--cycle,black); [/asy]\" width=\"952\" height=\"175\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7b617ac5c504bfcb033c29f4fd81bc01fe64f9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\frac{3}{8}\\qquad\\text{(B)}\\ \\frac{5}{27}\\qquad\\text{(C)}\\ \\frac{7}{16}\\qquad\\text{(D)}\\ \\frac{9}{16}\\qquad\\text{(E)}\\ \\frac{11}{45}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"389\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa62a365c27d4f2c298262b3e8c7c224550c20a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{th}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> triangle contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> rows of congruent smaller triangles, and for each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> inclusive, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f95e9fc37dc276d9cfc43aba335cde356371cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^{th}$\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> row contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> unshaded and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc6fab4c2fdb4e9046030fbfdcf6ea721b05602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> shaded small triangles.\n</p><p>Therefore, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da1fd13ee7c6d192c28bacb886ebddefa368cbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8^{th}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> triangle contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> rows, which contain a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/9/0790a5c6a6025fcd7c3fd25ae0f868639c31c9f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 + ... + 8 = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"185\" height=\"15\" /> unshaded small triangles and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef0ddba283371aa2b291d49c46e5aad2d17528e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 + 1 + 2 + ... + 7 = 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"185\" height=\"15\" /> shaded small triangles.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/84133c2fcf3f531f4b4c79c59a9c09ca820ae80f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{28}{28 + 36} = \\frac{28}{64} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{7}{16}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"203\" height=\"49\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da1fd13ee7c6d192c28bacb886ebddefa368cbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8^{th}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> triangle is shaded.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME\" title=\"1998 AJHSME\">1998 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1998\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"199